TY  - CONF
TI  - Language Embeddings for Typology and Cross-lingual Transfer Learning
AU  - Yu, Dian
AU  - He, Taiqi
AU  - Sagae, Kenji
PY  - 2021
AB  - Cross-lingual language tasks typically require a substantial amount of annotated data or parallel translation data. We explore whether language representations that capture relationships among languages can be learned and subsequently leveraged in cross-lingual tasks without the use of parallel data. We generate dense embeddings for 29 languages using a denoising autoencoder, and evaluate the embeddings using the World Atlas of Language Structures (WALS) and two extrinsic tasks in a zero-shot setting: cross-lingual dependency parsing and cross-lingual natural language inference.
